Nikki: update a subscription on a schedule

A subscription was downloaded only when Nikki started (with "Prefer: Remote") or when the user
pressed Update, so a provider's new servers or a renewed plan reached the router only after a
restart someone remembered to do.

Each subscription gets "Update automatically" and "Update every" (1, 3, 6 or 12 hours, or once
a day at 04:23) in its dialog on the Profiles page, and the Last update column says when it is
on. nikki.init writes one cron line per such subscription next to its scheduled restart (the
same #nikki tag, so stopping Nikki removes them with the others), calling a new extra command,
auto_update_subscription:

- a subscription that is not in use is downloaded, nothing else;
- the one in use is downloaded and Nikki restarted to run it, only when the download succeeded,
  so a failed download never takes the working profile away;
- the one in use with "Prefer: Remote" is not downloaded first, because the restart downloads it.

Applies to: https://github.com/nikkinikki-org/OpenWrt-nikki.git @ 0c56ba5f, after 0001.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

